         "<!-- res/xml/network_security_config.xml -->\n<network-security-config>\n    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted=\"false\">\n        <domain includeSubdomains=\"true\">api.example.com</domain>\n        <pin-set expiration=\"2027-01-01\">\n            <pin digest=\"SHA-256\">base64==</pin>\n            <pin digest=\"SHA-256\">backup==</pin> <!-- rotation -->\n        </pin-set>\n    </domain-config>\n</network-security-config>",
         "The config declares the policy as data: no cleartext to the API domain, a pin set with an expiration date and a backup pin for rotation. Review it like code — the expiration date is a calendar item, and the backup pin is what saves you when the primary certificate rotates unexpectedly.",
